    "working_name_not_printed": "자라는 구조를 살피는 식물 단면 드로잉",
    "whole_relationship": "A large observational drawing at the left connects leaf veins, branching stem, soil and roots in a cutaway pot, with a hand at the rim to establish attentive care and scale. The right Title/body/visit alignment may share M3’s effective reading structure; a fine drawn colour layer and different letter anatomy create its own style.",
    "positive_direction": "Precise botanical pen contour with translucent plum, lavender and muted rose wash on a cool pink ground. Let a few large leaves have generous colour depth while root/vein lines remain fine, legible and connected; use restrained crosshatching only where form needs it. A broad, clearly dominant Korean contrast-stroke Title and mature regular serif body create an observant editorial voice. Footer sans supports the serif reading with compatible optical size; no antique labels, distressed paper or decorative seal. Draw one substantial living plant through a clean observational cutaway: a coherent stem joins differently oriented leaves above soil, and believable roots branch through the soil below; a grown hand attends the pot rim. Do not add scientific labels, species names, measurements or invented horticultural facts. The pot cutaway is an image device for understanding care, not a technical promise. Show stem/root continuity, hand contact and variation in leaf anatomy, without converting the drawing into toy modelling or ornamental edge foliage.",
    "native_positive_brief": "Create one finished opaque flat landscape 16:9 poster. Use the supplied newly authored planning guide for actual copy anatomy, readable areas and substantive image contacts; implement the following completed style rather than reproducing its temporary shapes. Precise botanical pen contour with translucent plum, lavender and muted rose wash on a cool pink ground. Let a few large leaves have generous colour depth while root/vein lines remain fine, legible and connected; use restrained crosshatching only where form needs it. A broad, clearly dominant Korean contrast-stroke Title and mature regular serif body create an observant editorial voice. Footer sans supports the serif reading with compatible optical size; no antique labels, distressed paper or decorative seal. Draw one substantial living plant through a clean observational cutaway: a coherent stem joins differently oriented leaves above soil, and believable roots branch through the soil below; a grown hand attends the pot rim. Do not add scientific labels, species names, measurements or invented horticultural facts. The pot cutaway is an image device for understanding care, not a technical promise. Show stem/root continuity, hand contact and variation in leaf anatomy, without converting the drawing into toy modelling or ornamental edge foliage. A large observational drawing at the left connects leaf veins, branching stem, soil and roots in a cutaway pot, with a hand at the rim to establish attentive care and scale. The right Title/body/visit alignment may share M3’s effective reading structure; a fine drawn colour layer and different letter anatomy create its own style. The intended feeling is Curious, thoughtful and sensuous; a plant is a living structure to know and tend. Make the supplied main Title immediately recognisable through its broad size, weight/contrast and breathing space. Keep the market line as a subordinate eyebrow, the English name as a smaller companion, and the short explanatory sentence as a clear Subtitle. Keep the entire explanatory paragraph as mature regular body text with stable starts, natural Korean word spaces and meaning-led soft lines. Link its ending to the date/hour/place group, then nearby access/care information, invitation and URL along the same optical axis. Keep footer bodies clearly readable, with clean digits and original en-dashes drawn as distinct long midline bars. Choose harmonious Korean, Latin and numeral anatomy; image texture does not damage small text. All typography is part of the native finished image; do not add a later SVG/font overlay. Respect the supplied roles and all original punctuation without adding labels, numbers, logos, QR, watermarks or other print. This is a complete poster, with content-bearing imagery and precise letter finish. Print only the following twelve entries, each exactly once:\n\n집 안의 작은 숲\nLEAVES & LIVING\n초록을 고르고, 일상을 가꿉니다.\n작은 화분부터 오래 키운 나무까지 만납니다. 재배자의 이야기를 듣고, 우리 집의 빛과 생활에 맞는 식물을 골라보세요.\n성수 주말 식물 마켓\n2027.06.12–06.13\n토·일 11:00–19:00\n성수 온실마당\n입장 무료 · 분갈이 시연\n식물 구매 시 관리 안내 제공\n편하게 들러 천천히 둘러보세요.\nleaves.example/market",
